{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unwhite-worrying-bluebottle","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Parent\n\nEpic `77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec`, authorized at full scope by the operator on 2026-11-02.\nThis is deliverable 4.\n\n## Independent of the net-mechanism and sunset stories\n\nThose two edit the plan-review criteria registry. This one edits the CODE-REVIEW `tests`\ncriterion. Different gate, different rubric, no shared file — so it can run in parallel\nwith them.\n\n## The gap\n\nNo gate sees tests as complexity. The `tests` criterion on the code-review gate is\nADVISORY, and nothing anywhere asks whether a test is pinning BEHAVIOUR or merely pinning\nthe shape of a refactor.\n\nThe result is measurable in the tree the program just cleaned. Gate-induced tests the\ncomplexity-reduction program deleted included: four seam-guard modules written by\nmodule-size-cap split commits (2026-07-30, 08-13, 08-19); 88 held-out twins left behind by\nthe rebar-implement convention because it had no merge step; around 30 modules that\nre-ran lint scripts over the real tree; and CI-parity snapshot tests.\n\nEach of those was added in good faith to satisfy a gate. None of them tested a behaviour a\nuser could observe. They are a maintenance surface that grows every time a gate fires.\n\n## The change\n\nA test taxonomy, attached to the code-review `tests` criterion. Five shapes are named as\nNOT behaviour tests:\n\n1. pinning refactor mechanics (that a split happened, that a helper exists)\n2. pinning re-export identity (that `a.b` is the same object as `c.d`)\n3. pinning a LOC floor or ceiling on a file\n4. pinning import shape (that a module imports a particular way)\n5. re-running a gate script over the real tree\n\nA test of one of these shapes either carries an expiry, or it does not land.\n\nThe taxonomy describes shapes, not file names, so it does not need updating when files\nmove. It names the expiry as the escape hatch rather than banning the shapes outright,\nbecause some of them are legitimately useful for a short window during a migration.\n\n## Scope boundary\n\nThis story changes what the `tests` criterion ASKS. It does not change the criterion's\nposture from advisory to blocking — that is a separate judgement with its own blast\nradius, and bundling it here would make the red proofs ambiguous about which change did\nthe work.\n\n## Provider neutrality\n\nrebar must support a wide variety of providers and models. The taxonomy is rubric text and\nmust not assume a single vendor's model or tool-calling syntax.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The `tests` criterion's rubric names all 5 non-behaviour test shapes. Verified by\n      reading the rubric and by a test asserting each shape's name is present.\n- [ ] A change adding a test of each of the 5 shapes, with no expiry, produces a finding\n      from this criterion — one case per shape, 5 cases. Verified by tests.\n- [ ] A change adding a test of one of those shapes WITH an expiry produces no finding.\n      Verified by a test.\n- [ ] A change adding an ordinary behaviour test produces no finding. Verified by a test,\n      so the taxonomy is proven not to fire on normal work.\n- [ ] RED PROOF: one of the 4 named seam-guard modules, replayed as a change, produces a\n      finding. Verified by a test.\n- [ ] The criterion's posture is unchanged by this story. Verified by a test asserting it\n      is still advisory.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.\n\n## Plan grounding\n\nExact file:line citations for the `tests` criterion rubric, its routing entry, and the\ncode-review criteria overlay are being measured against `origin/main` and will be written\ninto this description before plan review is requested. This ticket is NOT ready for review\nuntil that is done.","id":"f86e-b57b-008d-4652","parent_id":"77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Add a test taxonomy to the code-review tests criterion: mechanics-pinning tests carry an expiry or do not land"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793647980812182766,"uuid":"bb52a961-e9b4-4d37-be01-ca6e23a575cf"}